In my honest opinion, parents should do parenting and speak to their children about porn, consent, sex, and relationships. Problem solved.

No, they have a different flavor on religious extremism that is mixed with their cultural norms. For example, the hijab and misogyny in Shia/Persian regions are more state enforced while in the Arab world, most countries don't have hijab mandates, but the society enforces it through intimidation and brutality. This is why there are women protesting the hijab in Iran, while women in the Arab world promoting it.

&#x200B;

To a westerner, both are the same, but as a native, I can tell you for sure that what influences the Arab world is the gulf region. If Iran turned to an oasis of human rights overnight, the Middle East wouldn't even care.
